  "briefing": {
    "headline": "Hogs near $56 as pork cutout slips; export sales due 7:30",
    "lead": "December hogs settled at $56.03 while the national cash hog price sat at $43.25. That gap is about $12.78 a hundredweight, and futures buyers are paying well over what packers paid on the kill.",
    "teaser": "Futures hogs sit near $56 while cash hogs trade near $43, with export sales due this morning.",
    "one_number": {
      "value": "462,000",
      "unit": "hogs killed Wednesday, USDA estimate",
      "context": "That is 33,000 fewer than a week ago and 25,293 fewer than a year ago, a lighter kill on the day."
    },
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Hogs: futures above cash",
        "body": "- December hogs settled Wednesday at **$56.03**, up 0.4% from Tuesday's $55.80.\n- USDA AMS put national negotiated cash hogs at $43.25 carcass base on 3,605 head killed Nov 10; the pork cutout was $69.34.",
        "so_what": "Futures and cash are far apart this morning.",
        "conviction_level": "low",
        "overnight_surprise": false
      },
      {
        "title": "Grains: corn flat, beans soft",
        "body": "- December corn is at **$4.48** overnight, unchanged from Wednesday's settle.\n- January soybeans are at $12.28¾, down 2 cents. USDA AMS had Gulf corn bids at 94 to 95 over December on Wednesday.",
        "so_what": "Quiet board ahead of the export sales report.",
        "conviction_level": "low",
        "overnight_surprise": false
      },
      {
        "title": "Cattle and crude",
        "body": "- December live cattle settled Wednesday at **$218.98**, down 0.1%, and feeders gained 0.7% to $332.63.\n- WTI is at $86.04 overnight, down 0.6%, as Asian reports said Iran and Ukraine peace hopes are building.",
        "so_what": "Feeders firmed while fats cattle barely moved.",
        "conviction_level": "low",
        "overnight_surprise": false
      }
    ],
